Parity arithmetic reproduced exactly from the web source (cross-platform value parity, NOT a "corrected"
version):
  distance      = convertDistanceFromSI(d.distance_m ?? 0, unitPref) [ /1000 km · /1609.344 mi · /0.3048 ft ]
                  then fmtNumber(dist, 1)
  duration      = formatDurationMinutes((d.duration_s ?? 0)/60, { subMinuteLabel:'<1m' })
                  [ '—' for non-finite/negative · '<1m' for <1 · 'Hh Mm' / 'Mm' with minutes rounded en-US ]
  address       = truncateAddress(addr, 30)  [ '—' for missing/empty · slice(0,30)+'…' for over-long ]
  SoC           = `${start ?? '?'}% → ${end ?? '?'}%`
  battery used  = (start != null && end != null) ? fmtInt(start-end)+'%' : null, shown only when dist > 0
  date          = formatDateShort(d.start_ts)  [ '—' for missing · locale+tz { month:'short', day:'numeric' } ]
  driveLimit    = isWide(cols>=3) ? 10 : isTall(rows>=2) ? 7 : 5 ; address column shown only when isWide

States reproduced (every one renders — no hidden surfaces):
  loading (skeleton list) · empty ("No recent drives recorded") · error (retry) · stale (chip + banner +
  auto-refresh) · offline (cached rows + banner) · content (responsive list). Each has a #if DEBUG preview.

